# La Boom's bartender. Client of "Bar Tab": Dec Vega owes him 400 sat.
# Flags: b_bar_tab_accepted, bar_tab(paid|instalments|written_off), b_bar_tab_lie_failed. Reacts to Killed(dec_vega).

%rec: OpeningBranch

cond: HasFlag('Killed(dec_vega)') && !HasFlag('bar_tab(paid)')
goto: VegaDead

cond: HasFlag('bar_tab(paid)') || HasFlag('bar_tab(instalments)') || HasFlag('bar_tab(written_off)')
goto: Done

cond: HasFlag('b_bar_tab_accepted')
goto: Return

cond: true
goto: Default

%rec: Nodes

name: Default
npc: (He polishes a glass that is already clean.) What'll it be?
#
o_text: Show me the drinks.
o_id: drinks
o_effect: StartTrading
o_goto: Default
#
o_text: You look like a man with a problem.
o_id: ask_job
o_goto: Job
#
o_text: Nothing.
o_id: bye
o_goto: End

name: Job
npc: Dec Vega. Drinks here every night, pays never. Four hundred sat on the slate.
+ He sits with the Cognetic Bastards across the street. Bring me my four hundred and 150 of it is yours.
#
o_text: Done.
o_id: accept_tab
o_goto: Accepted
#
o_text: Not my kind of work.
o_id: decline_tab
o_goto: End

name: Return
npc: Dec's four hundred. You have it?
#
o_text: Here. Four hundred.
o_id: pay_tab
o_cond: HasItem('gold', 400)
o_goto: Paid
#
o_text: Dec's wallet. Four hundred, count it.
o_id: pay_wallet
o_cond: HasItem('vega_wallet')
o_goto: PaidWallet
#
o_text: He'll pay in instalments. Fifty a week. He means it.
o_id: instalments
o_cond: HasFlag('b_vega_instalments')
o_goto: Instalments
#
o_text: Dec is broke. Flat. You'll never see that money; write it off.
o_id: write_off
o_cond: HasFlag('b_vega_sided') && !HasFlag('b_bar_tab_lie_failed')
o_test: RollSkill('social', 'Hard')
o_succ: WrittenOff
o_fail: LieFailed
#
o_text: Show me the drinks.
o_id: drinks_return
o_effect: StartTrading
o_goto: Return
#
o_text: Working on it.
o_id: working
o_goto: End

name: Paid
npc: (He counts it twice.) Huh. Didn't think he had it in him. Or you in you.
+ Hundred and fifty, as agreed. First drink's on the house.
effect: StackTransferTo(NPC, 'gold', 400)
effect: PlayerAddGold(150)
effect: SetFlag('bar_tab(paid)')
#
o_text: Pleasure.
o_id: paid_bye
o_goto: End

name: PaidWallet
npc: (He knows the wallet. He counts it anyway.) Four hundred. Hundred and fifty of it is yours, as agreed.
+ Don't come to my bar with his wallet again.
effect: StackTransferTo(NPC, 'vega_wallet')
effect: PlayerAddGold(150)
effect: SetFlag('bar_tab(paid)')
#
o_text: Pleasure.
o_id: paid_wallet_bye
o_goto: End

name: Instalments
npc: Instalments. (A long breath.) Fine. Fifty a week, and the first week he misses I send someone less polite than you.
+ Half your fee. The other half when he's paid up, which will be never.
effect: PlayerAddGold(75)
effect: SetFlag('bar_tab(instalments)')
#
o_text: Fair enough.
o_id: instalments_bye
o_goto: End

name: WrittenOff
npc: (He looks at you for a long moment, then wipes the slate.) Broke. Of course he is. The whole street is.
+ Written off. Don't expect a fee for bringing me nothing.
effect: SetFlag('bar_tab(written_off)')
#
o_text: Didn't.
o_id: written_off_bye
o_goto: End

name: LieFailed
npc: Broke? He bought a round for the Bastards last Tuesday. Don't carry his water in my bar.
+ Four hundred. Or nothing for you either.
effect: SetFlag('b_bar_tab_lie_failed')
#
o_text: Fine.
o_id: lie_failed_bye
o_goto: End

name: VegaDead
npc: (He doesn't look up.) Dec's dead. Heard it from three people before noon.
+ Four hundred sat. That's what he was worth to somebody.
#
o_text: His wallet. Four hundred, count it.
o_id: pay_wallet_dead
o_cond: HasItem('vega_wallet') && HasFlag('b_bar_tab_accepted')
o_goto: PaidWallet
#
o_text: Show me the drinks.
o_id: drinks_dead
o_effect: StartTrading
o_goto: VegaDead
#
o_text: (Leave.)
o_id: dead_bye
o_goto: End

name: Done
npc: Back again. The slate's clean, the glasses aren't.
#
o_text: Show me the drinks.
o_id: drinks_done
o_effect: StartTrading
o_goto: Done
#
o_text: Later.
o_id: done_bye
o_goto: End

name: Accepted
npc: Four hundred. Not three-ninety.
effect: SetFlag('b_bar_tab_accepted')
effect: EndConversation

name: End
npc: (He goes back to his glass.)
effect: EndConversation
